e, fixed-size, randomly connected hidden layer called a \"reservoir,\" which processes input data. The weights of the reservoir are typically fixed, and only the output weights are trained using a simple linear regression. Training involves exposing the reservoir to input data and adjusting the output weights to minimize prediction error.\n\nThe summaries of the arXiv papers did not contain relevant information about echo state networks for anomaly detection. The Wikipedia article provides a basic understanding of how ESNs are trained.","role":"assistant"},"model":"qwen2.5:7b","prompt_eval_count":773,"prompt_eval_duration":244192000,"total_duration":1570457900}}